  "summary_en": "KIEP briefing on the US and global humanoid robot industry and the second Trump administration's policy: AI support, deregulation, export controls and investment limits on China, onshoring, and proposed congressional bills. It draws implications for Korea: standards and safety, physical-AI capability building, K-Humanoid Alliance support, and labor transition.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Global humanoid market is forecast to grow from $2.02B (2024) to $15.26B (2030), a 39.2% CAGR.",
   "The US leads in AI chips and models; China leads in hardware supply chains and produced 87% of 2025 humanoid shipments.",
   "Trump administration policy: deregulation, export controls, outbound investment limits, procurement bans on Chinese firms, and a possible robotics executive order in 2026.",
   "New humanoid safety standard ISO 25785-1 is under development, since ISO 10218 and ISO/TS 15066 do not cover humanoids.",
   "Korea should develop regulation, insurance and liability schemes, ethics guidelines, and workforce retraining as humanoids move into services and care."
  ],
